@startuml
title New Local File Upload Flow
start

note right
  This path handles local files that are not yet tracked as an
  existing canonical DriveItem. A same-name online object is not
  automatically safe to overwrite; it becomes a reconciliation case.
end note

if (Path is protected by .nosync?) then (yes)
  :Skip upload;
  stop
endif

:Resolve parent DB identity / target drive;
if (Parent cannot be resolved?) then (yes)
  :Record upload failure;
  stop
endif

if (Local file still exists and is readable?) then (no)
  :Treat disappeared file as no-op,\nor unreadable file as failure;
  stop
endif

:Read file size;
if (Exceeds Microsoft maximum upload size?) then (yes)
  :Record upload failure;
  stop
endif

:Check cached / available OneDrive quota where available;
if (Known insufficient online space?) then (yes)
  :Record upload failure;
  stop
endif

:Query target name online;
if (Same-name online item exists?) then (yes)
  :Validate case-sensitive/POSIX naming compatibility;
  if (Local content matches online item?) then (yes)
    :Zero data traversal;
    :Save online identity / metadata in DB;
    note right
      Matching bytes can be bound to the existing online identity;
      there is no reason to upload or create a conflict copy.
    end note
    stop
  else (no)
    :Treat collision as existing-file reconciliation;
    :Temporarily establish online identity in DB;
    :Evaluate local versus current online state;
    if (Local version is selected for modified upload?) then (yes)
      :Route to modified-file upload path;
    else (no / conflict)
      :Create verified independent safeBackup copy;
      note right
        LOCAL DATA LOSS PREVENTION

        The local candidate must not be discarded merely because the
        same pathname already exists online. Preserve the local bytes
        before resolving which object remains canonical.
      end note
      :Upload safeBackup as a new file;
      :Remove temporary canonical DB association;
      if (~--upload-only?) then (yes)
        :Retain canonical local file for future reconciliation;
        note right
          ~--upload-only cannot apply the online version locally, so
          the canonical local path is retained after preservation.
        end note
      else (no)
        :Download authoritative online file transactionally;
        note right
          In bidirectional operation the online canonical can now be
          applied locally because the differing local bytes have been
          preserved independently.
        end note
      endif
    endif
    stop
  endif
else (404 / no existing item)
  :Proceed with actual new-file upload;
endif

if (File is zero bytes?) then (yes)
  :Use simple upload;
else (no)
  if (force_session_upload or\n~--upload-only + ~--local-first?) then (yes)
    :Use upload session;
  else (no)
    if (File <= session threshold?) then (yes)
      :Use simple upload;
    else (no)
      :Use resumable upload session;
    endif
  endif
endif

:Validate upload response and content integrity;
if (Simple upload succeeded and integrity passed?) then (yes)
  :Save Microsoft-returned metadata;
  if (Not ~--upload-only?) then (yes)
    :Apply Microsoft-returned timestamp locally;
  endif
else (session / enrichment handling)
  :Apply session-upload and account-specific\npost-upload reconciliation rules;
  if (SharePoint enrichment changed uploaded content?) then (yes)
    if (Bidirectional mode and no new-version override?) then (yes)
      :Download Microsoft-returned enriched file transactionally;
    else (no)
      :Apply configured metadata/version reconciliation;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Save successful upload state;
  endif
endif

stop
@enduml
